{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1794528022, "title": "game/puzzle \u00b7 not-ambitious run 1", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "theme": {"fg": "#d8dee9", "bg": "#1e1f1c", "palette": "#272822:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f8f8f2:#75715e:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f9f8f5"}}
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Make an original puzzle game I can play in the browser, as a single web page\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[15.795, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I'll build a twin-mirror puzzle: you move two avatars at once, and one of them moves horizontally mirrored.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll check every level with a solver before finishing.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.493, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/mirror-twins/index.html)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[48.668, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 2 files\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/check.js)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[50.043, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 2 files, ran 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(node <workspace>/check.js \"<workspace>/mirror-twins/index.html\")\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[56.752, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Levels 6 and 7 are unsolvable, and 3 and 8 are too easy. I'll rework those four.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
