[65.206, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The two twins' x-coordinates always sum to the same total unless a move gets blocked. Level 6's goals break\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  that invariant, so I'll fix them and rework level 7.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[66.339, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd <workspace> && python3 - <<'E')\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[71.484, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I made **Mirror Twins**, a browser puzzle game in one HTML file. I haven't played it in a browser, so the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  drawing, input handling and level menu are untested. I did check all 10 levels with a solver, and each one\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  can be solved.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **How it plays:** Arrow keys or WASD (or a swipe on touch) move both twins at the same time. The orange twin\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  moves as you press. The blue twin moves **mirrored left–right**, so pressing right sends it left. Put each\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  twin on its matching dashed ring. Along the way:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Crates can be pushed, and the twins block each other.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Spikes kill a twin, so you have to undo.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A wall can block one twin while the other still moves, which shifts them out of step. Most levels depend\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  on that.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Z undoes and R resets. The game shows your move count against the shortest solution, and your best score\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and progress are saved in the browser.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Solver results:** the shortest solutions range from 2 to 10 moves. Levels 8 to 10 are shorter than I'd\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  like for late levels, so the difficulty curve is a bit flat. If you want it harder, I can make the late\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  levels longer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  To play, open `<workspace>/mirror-twins/index.html` in a browser. The solver I used to check the levels is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `<workspace>/check.js`. It isn't part of the game.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[76.054, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Push it further.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[78.652, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRead 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Read(<workspace>/mirror-twins/index.html)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[87.695, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I'll push it in three directions: a new mechanic (pressure plates and doors), a generator that searches for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  hard levels, and polish (smooth movement, sound, win screen). I'm starting with the rules.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
